  "evaluation_notes": [
    "Every TrashNet image is included. Paths stay in the original folders; image_root is data/ so filepath can reach both trees.",
    "TrashNet cardboard, glass, paper, and cans map to those BinSight classes. Plastic bottles stay plastic_bottle_jug. Clamshells, cups, tubs, lids, and loose caps are other_rigid_plastic. Bags and bubble mailers are plastic_film. Chip bags, foil, and oil jugs are other_landfill. Food scraps in the trash folder are food_organic.",
    "other_rigid_plastic, plastic_film, and food_organic get some TrashNet images. battery_electronics stays BinSight-only. train.py class weights rebalance the loss.",
    "Splits are still by item_id. A BinSight capture stays together. Each TrashNet image is its own item, so those images scatter across train, val, and test."
